<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France: Thousands march in Orléans against National Rally congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4143236f292cdb12885b671c40d3fd4f25e03c119385d11e53f4fa36f4b2b05</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:45:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261024-france-thousands-march-in-orl_ans-against-national-rally-congress--f231df26b1ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261024-france-thousands-march-in-orl%C3%A9ans-against-national-rally-congress" /><summary type="html">Thousands of anti-fascist protesters took to the streets of Orléans on Saturday to demonstrate against a congress held by Marine Le Pen’s far-right National Rally party. Marchers criticised both Le Pen and President Emmanuel Macron, chanting slogans and carrying banners opposing the far right. The protest came amid renewed nationwide demonstrations over the cost of living, a week after rallies descended into street violence. The two-day congress also marked a major campaign event for Le Pen ahead of France’s presidential election in six months’ time. Antonia Kerrigan reports the latest from Orleans.</summary></entry><entry><title>US seeks to topple Cuba's government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3974b2eac28ee1ed58ff96c14b7f370d104a28903d73c1f842b7e14ff71490d</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:43:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government--b52eb58eab6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government" /><summary type="html">And now, in a rather surprising development, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is directly urging Cubans to cooperate with the CIA. Havana has responded by mocking what it calls the Trump administration’s “desperation”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump challenges Alaska Senate trace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98f0f6a086b42d3587494102a2e2b2a8cdbe6313930f5c4c27f79a832c519219</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace--8639a06bdbc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections less than two weeks away, concerns are growing over whether President Donald Trump would accept a major Republican defeat. Trump has called for legal action to block the certification of Alaska’s Senate race if Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan loses to his Democratic challenger, Mary Peltola, arguing that another candidate with the same name on the ballot could confuse voters. Our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Young demonstrators demand concrete action from Macron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b73b32f3e8a85d5fb3cd673cae15fa492a93d901739a628d3f2dc4c59f45bc2d</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:41:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-young-demonstrators-demand-concrete-action-from-macron--d1843bce28f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-young-demonstrators-demand-concrete-action-from-macron" /><summary type="html">Student protests in France began more than a month ago, over poor conditions in high schools, teacher shortages, the pace of the school day and inequalities between private and public education. The movement has since grown into a broader mobilisation, bringing together the Yellow Vests, trade unions and wider civil society. Joseph Downing, Senior lecturer in politics and international relations and Aston University, shares further details,</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump administration sues to block possible Democratic win in Alaska Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67beebaed056e68ead9fd7ecc6d745ae8397242c54037bba253854bd5189f265</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race--2cdc4eae1c83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that he had instructed his administration to file a lawsuit to block the certification of the US Senate race in Alaska if Republican Senator Dan Sullivan loses, arguing that voters would be confused because two Republicans on the ballot have similar names. The legal battle is ramping up questions over whether Trump will accept a potential midterms defeat.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France braces for new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26e4f5bb0fe73c449d1e57bb0a3419139b4968d03471ac7a416d6afe2e70e916</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:36:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-new-protests--c859d296b05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-new-protests" /><summary type="html">A coalition of the “Yellow Vests” movement, trade unions and students will march across France on Saturday with demands over studying conditions and purchasing power. Some 70,000 police are expected to be deployed as authorities fear looting and vandalism similar to last Saturday's unrest. Story by J. Pownall, S. Perez, M. Bougault.</summary></entry><entry><title>NFL would cancel Paris game if unsafe due to protests, Steelers QB Aaron Rodgers says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91bc22311ce02fff521136f3c972bfcca215f3418297f07f36e6cb9604133bc0</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:36:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261024-nfl-would-cancel-paris-game-if-unsafe-due-to-protests-steelers-qb-aaron-rodgers-says--6f44dda85056.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261024-nfl-would-cancel-paris-game-if-unsafe-due-to-protests-steelers-qb-aaron-rodgers-says" /><summary type="html">Pittsburgh Steelers quarterback Aaron Rodgers said Friday the NFL would have cancelled its first regular-season game in Paris if the situation were unsafe due to recent mass protests. The Steelers are scheduled to face the New Orleans Saints at the Stade de France in the Paris suburb of ​Saint-Denis on Sunday.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6b4ff968e44f76287e05003d1d6636847b624757b614f8a3511c9d1470d638e</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation--93ec6832b46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation" /><summary type="html">Israel has imposed widespread closures across the occupied West Bank and displaced residents following attacks by Palestinian gunmen that killed two Israeli soldiers. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu visited the site of the attack near Hebron and instructed security forces to immediately cordon off the city. Morgan Ayre reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d39cebcdb61d38feaccb798622e6952ecf265c9fe406fe6d5f159e2121c2ff5b</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan--3f52c552700e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan" /><summary type="html">Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students vow to keep protesting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f204eff4adbf7fd10ff35d398a0c626b3852e1b19dea8dda9dad2e3f5ee3c316</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:31:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-students-vow-to-keep-protesting--f3e830e86996.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-students-vow-to-keep-protesting" /><summary type="html">Amid growing concerns over violence, people across France, young and old alike, are weighing up whether taking part in demonstrations is worth the risk. France 24’s Ophelie Jackson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: March against National Rally in Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e84c89ec6bd75e030525d5e9319dfe0ba1e66ffbbff3d4a45da31cc318deae29</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:30:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-march-against-national-rally-in-orleans--8c43102911ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-march-against-national-rally-in-orleans" /><summary type="html">Against this backdrop of heightened tensions, France’s far-right National Rally is holding its annual congress in Orléans, south of Paris, where it is expected to officially launch Marine Le Pen’s presidential campaign and re-elect Jordan Bardella as party leader. Thousands of supporters are expected to attend, while a major counter-demonstration has been organised against racism, fascism and imperialism. Local authorities are preparing for possible clashes between the two groups. Antonia Kerrigan reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris: Last-minute change to the protest route</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f23bce573c9ea84d484ce0340229870fbc1cc547e60cee78cc4a81e64eae9e</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:29:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-last-minute-change-to-the-protest-route--0197c0cde6d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-last-minute-change-to-the-protest-route" /><summary type="html">The Paris police prefecture changed the route of the authorised trade union march at the last minute ahead of the 24 October mobilisation.

The new route runs between Place d’Italie and Porte de Vincennes. But this morning, many protesters turned up at Place de la Bastille, the march’s original starting point, before the route was changed, leaving them confused and unsure where to go.

France 24 journalist Elitsa Gadeva brings us the latest from the scene.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink and Starshield connection 'stable' again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5862b8afaa76749954cb52f50e488e6f43a5f64379bde2754431de3d4e3b6d89</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T09:48:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-ukraine-says-starlink-and-starshield-connection-stable-again--c2932aea6b3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-ukraine-says-starlink-and-starshield-connection-stable-again" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has regained a "stable" connection to the Starlink and Starshield satellite communications systems, Kyiv's defence minister said on Saturday. Recent disruptions to the connection led to tensions with Washington over the SpaceX-made network crucial to the Ukrainian army's operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Protests against cost of living expected in Italy under heavy security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b43b67da23d7ba6dc5b74d92fc6478b8cbd35b906c97432f521776338551af2a</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T07:08:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-protests-against-cost-of-living-expected-in-italy-under-heavy-security--6332b0b26bda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-protests-against-cost-of-living-expected-in-italy-under-heavy-security" /><summary type="html">Italy is preparing for another day of protests on Saturday against budget cuts and the high cost of living in eight cities, including Rome and Milan. Following last weekend’s unrest, authorities announced heavy security measures, including the use of drones and helicopters to monitor the marches.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police deploy in large numbers, major Paris museums close ahead of new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd62feb978314fa31a1b471df504f2f3bb8fa93abfca815fbbdbfdc41a21d921</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:27:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-french-police-deploy-in-big-numbers-and-paris-shuts-major-museums-ahead-of-new-protests--89e1425011b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-french-police-deploy-in-big-numbers-and-paris-shuts-major-museums-ahead-of-new-protests" /><summary type="html">France will deploy about 70,000 police nationwide and some of Paris' major museums will close Saturday as the country braces for a fresh wave of protests after looting and unrest erupted on the sidelines of demonstrations a week ago. Another massive turnout is expected after more than a half million took to the streets last week.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Live: French police seize weapons and arrest 135 people on the sidelines of new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b81399188d643bcce68a4111ec81191ca3d8a59b5de739b28e55c0d2dd1dedcc</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T04:59:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-live-hundreds-of-protests-expected-in-france-amid-high-tensions-and-heavy-police-presence--fda62057d1da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-live-hundreds-of-protests-expected-in-france-amid-high-tensions-and-heavy-police-presence" /><summary type="html">Police have seized various weapons and arrested 135 people on the sidelines of new protests on Saturday, French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez said. Some 70,000 police have been deployed ahead of a march by “Yellow Vests”, trade unions and students, with authorities fearing a repeat of the looting and vandalism seen during last Saturday's unrest. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says US may launch ‘another little Epic Fury’ attack on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef4e0f38dee098fb2107a313368fd0129e805597222aa1e3360a03e632ede273</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:50:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran--267a801616fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said his country may launch “another little Epic Fury” on Iran, referring to the joint Israeli-American military operation that sparked the war with Iran at the end of February.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Building collapse in Nairobi search for survivors under way</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b1d1957c6b38f6e95e688f1c4cc80ea6da2787259532b3b308bfb03e2fd8aa2</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:31:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way--5d7e9d1e7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, scramble to get through rubble to trapped survivors after a more than 10 storeys building being built in Nairobi goes down.  Also, Kenya says that there's been a second Ebola death. Earlier this week it had logged 9 cases so far, all traced back to its first Ebola patient who died earlier this month. And in finally the 11th edition of the iconic contemporary art festival Also known as Africa taking place in Paris, we speak to Cape Verde's artist Amadeo Carvalho.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>After French Riots, Curfews &amp; Calm .. is a new Storm Brewing ? Plus Ukraine &amp; Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30e32464649791b6d987ac4af59f2e665215ff939e2f4a3408251692aa119b52</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261023-after-french-riots-curfews-calm-is-a-new-storm-brewing-plus-ukraine-israel--493a50160c77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261023-after-french-riots-curfews-calm-is-a-new-storm-brewing-plus-ukraine-israel" /><summary type="html">It's been a week that’s seen mass protests hijacked by violent rioters across France. The looting of shops, trashing of public buildings, the burning of Lyon’s Tourist Information and the iconic Limoges City Hall.  After the riots, came the curfews, and the contemplation, who did what and why weren’t they stopped. Seditious groups, ultra left anarchists and opportunist criminals said President Macron, with a qualified mea culpa: failures in anticipation and authorities dropped the ball in intelligence gathering. Macron is out of breath,  exhausted and disorientated claimed the Presidential Frontrunner Marine Le Pen, the far right leader now polling in an even stronger position for the Presidency. Foreign leaders had a free for all too, President Trump wading in and Israel’s prime minister settled old scores ahead of elections there. But France wasn’t isolated in its protests and unrest, Milan was a mirror image, with demonstrations in Spain, Portugal, Belgium too, An Autumn of Discontent, and more protests to follow this weekend:</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu weighs West Bank operation ahead of elections: ‘Politically, it will not help anybody’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:315717ec41c2c8e8f2f1c5e8a326e98bc55e1381b58fd7c686cf5b86f5e1dd02</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:26:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybod--82f68804f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybody" /><summary type="html">As Israel approaches a consequential parliamentary election amid renewed violence in the occupied West Bank, Yedioth Ahronoth Senior Journalist Ben-Dror Yemini offers a critical assessment of Benjamin Netanyahu's political prospects, the limits of military escalation and the shifting relationship between national security and electoral legitimacy.
 
Since October 7, 2023 "Netanyahu is not popular anymore," Yemini argues, identifying the Hamas-led attacks as a decisive turning point in the Israeli prime minister's public standing.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>How Israeli settlers wearing keffiyehs are attacking West Bank olive groves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4e255bd4725b9d125da73a6fb5b611c07a3ef3c39f10b20d06a7107295c4da1</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves--10563b4076b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves" /><summary type="html">The olive harvest officially began in the West Bank on October 15, 2026, and it has coincided with an uptick in violence towards Palestinians carried out by both Israeli settlers and soldiers. Meanwhile, the settlers and soldiers have been using social media to promote an aesthetic, Instagram-friendly and nationalistic view of these harvests.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: Could Arab parties play kingmaker in the next Knesset ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffc22ad45e20492fa8abcb5b9f6efd6b186821172a228f83003cafbe7963c36</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset--cd40bcd2e863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls for the first legislative election since Hamas's October 7 attacks, neither Prime Minister Benjamin #Netanyahu's Likud party nor former army chief of staff Gadi #Eisenkot's Yashar party are likely to win a majority of seats in the #Knesset. Turns out, #Israel's Arab parties could have a say in the election's outcome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza : digging up the bodies from under the rubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e7842ac4a0455a6c8d234f116242cd457e940dcc5dd9b69f36bdb0287353c8</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:10:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261023-gaza-digging-up-the-bodies-from-under-the-rubble--7e525732a26a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261023-gaza-digging-up-the-bodies-from-under-the-rubble" /><summary type="html">One year after the ceasefire in Gaza, efforts to recover the bodies buried beneath the rubble are continuing. Civil Defense officials say 1,000 bodies have been recovered so far, but the task remains immense: between 8,000 and 10,000 more are still believed to be buried under the debris, including 3,000 in areas controlled by the Israeli army.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: France’s Macron arrives in Trappes after ‘racist terrorist attack’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c9930c5b555c81ed42587c3a466cf992eaef18176701b37005bb76c6d15a867</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:08:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack--4e9b6abddebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack" /></entry></feed>
